course: dictionary
lesson: 14753
title: A word for habits: propensity
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Propensity is a formal word. It means a natural habit of behaving in a certain way, a tendency. If someone has a propensity to do something, they often do it without even trying.
explain: Look at the clues in «Ruby has a propensity to tell jokes.» Ruby tells jokes a lot, so this is a habit of hers. Try swapping in a simpler word: «Ruby has a tendency to tell jokes» works well, so propensity is close in meaning to tendency.
explain: The words after propensity show you how to use it. «A propensity to» is followed by an action, as in «a propensity to get lost». «A propensity for» is followed by a noun or an -ing word, as in «a propensity for getting lost».
explain: In science, propensity can also mean how likely something is to happen. «Wet paper has a propensity to tear» means wet paper is likely to tear. The clues are the words around it, just like with any other new word.
fact: Propensity is a noun, and it is a formal word. You will meet it more in reports and older books than in everyday chat.
fact: «Propensity» means a natural tendency to behave in a certain way.
fact: «A propensity to» is followed by a verb, and «a propensity for» is followed by a noun or an -ing word.
fact: In science, propensity can mean how likely something is to happen.
fact: A simple synonym for propensity is tendency.
exercise: «Our dog has a propensity to dig holes in the garden.» What does propensity mean here? | A sudden loud noise | *A natural habit of doing something | A kind of food | A large garden with lots of holes
exercise: «Mia has a propensity for getting lost in new places.» Which phrase is closest in meaning? | A plan to visit new places | A map of the town | *A tendency to get lost
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to propensity? | Shadow | *Tendency | Pencil | Journey
test: «Ben has a propensity to forget his homework.» Ben often forgets his homework. What does this tell you? | *He often forgets, as a habit | He has lost his school bag | He forgot once, by accident | He never forgets
test: «The metal has a propensity to rust in wet weather.» In science, what does this sentence mean? | *The metal is likely to rust in wet weather | The metal is shiny and new | The metal cannot be painted | The metal rusts only in the sun
exam: Which sentence uses propensity correctly? | Lena ate a propensity of cake. | *Lena has a propensity to sing loudly in the bath. | The propensity sang Lena a song. | Lena has a propensity for the blue bus.
